  "sourceInterpretation": "Official image reports IDFv6.1-dirty with unknown private revision. Fixed public fff9895c82d744c7237be8847347bdd1b07c6643 establishes control bits,reset values,wait fields,threshold transaction and source143. Functional detector-edge qualification is explicitly supplied,not a voltage waveform,measured oscillator or silicon validation of latency/order.",
  "semantics": {
    "mode0": "Independent mode0 control/reset/wait fields and HP/LP RAW/ENA/ST/CLR. Counter-clear is RW level. No progress from reads,zero edges,held clear or disabled detection. Explicit active detector samples accumulate wait; inactive samples reset qualification. RAW can reassert on later edges if condition persists; separate banks acknowledge independently.",
    "routing": "Actual enabled HP raw event -> source143 -> per-hart matrix/CLIC. LP registers retained,no LP processor route claimed.",
    "reset": "Digital-system reset selection produces existing PowerReset(Brownout) diagnostic stop. No implicit host reset or claimed physical reset pulse.",
    "analog": "Target0x61,register5,threshold bits2:0; fullbyte seed required because reset unspecified. Guest transactions obey existing parent/master/slave routes and preserve unknown bits via RMW. No voltage conversion.",
    "unsupported": [
      "Unknown FIB-controlled policy",
      "Active higher-priority analog mode1 in mode0 input path",
      "Chip-wide analog reset on a real event",
      "Flash/RF shutdown on a real event",
      "Physical voltage threshold and detector clock rate",
      "LP processor interrupt handling",
      "Complete Plus board/display"
    ]
  },
